---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
const sections = [
  { id: 'preferences', title: 'Your analytics choice' }, { id: 'storage', title: 'Cookies and browser storage' },
  { id: 'analytics', title: 'Optional analytics' }, { id: 'security', title: 'Contact-form protection' },
  { id: 'app-widget', title: 'The app and widget' }, { id: 'browser-controls', title: 'Browser controls' },
];
---
<LegalLayout title="Cookie Policy" description="What this website stores in your browser, why it is used, and how to control optional analytics." sections={sections}>
  <div class="legal-summary"><h2>Analytics is your choice.</h2><p>You can use this website without Google Analytics. The analytics script loads only after you choose to allow it. Essential settings and contact-form security are separate from that choice.</p></div>
  <section id="preferences"><h2>Your analytics choice</h2><p>Allow or reject optional Google Analytics for this browser on this website. Both choices leave the site available. You can change your choice here or through “Cookie settings” in the footer.</p><div class="legal-cookie-options"><button type="button" data-analytics-choice="rejected" hidden>Reject analytics</button><button type="button" data-analytics-choice="accepted" hidden>Allow analytics</button></div><p class="legal-cookie-status" data-cookie-status role="status" aria-live="polite">Analytics is off unless you choose to allow it.</p><noscript><p>JavaScript is disabled, so this website does not load Google Analytics. No analytics choice is needed.</p></noscript></section>
  <section id="storage"><h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2><p>Cookies are small values a website stores in your browser and can receive with requests. Local storage keeps values for a website in your browser without automatically sending them with each request.</p><div class="legal-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Browser storage details"><table><thead><tr><th>Storage</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>replaid-analytics-consent-v1</code></td><td>Local storage that remembers your analytics choice.</td><td>Valid for 180 days, or until you clear it. We ask again after it expires.</td></tr><tr><td><code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_T2C7LJY6CL</code></td><td>Google Analytics cookies used only after you allow analytics.</td><td>Configured for up to 180 days. Later activity can renew them while consent remains valid.</td></tr><tr><td><code>theme</code></td><td>A display preference saved by the earlier site design. The current pages use the light design.</td><td>Until you remove it through browser settings.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Security providers may also use browser storage when you use protected features such as the contact form. Their storage is described below.</p></section>
  <section id="analytics"><h2>Optional analytics</h2><p>Google Analytics helps us understand visits and use of the public website. It can process page visits, browser and device information, cookie identifiers, and network information. The site sends page addresses without query strings or fragments and does not intentionally send contact-form messages to Analytics.</p><p>If you reject analytics or have not made a choice, we do not load the Google Analytics script. If you withdraw a previous choice, we disable further collection by this site's tag and remove its accessible Analytics cookies. This does not delete information already received by Google.</p><p>Your choice is saved for this browser and website, not for other devices or the separate Replaid application. If browser storage is blocked, a choice can apply to the current page but may not be remembered on the next visit.</p><p>We do not enable advertising personalization in this site's Analytics configuration. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses data from partner sites</a> for Google's processing details.</p></section>
  <section id="security"><h2>Contact-form protection</h2><p>The contact page uses Web3Forms for message delivery and hCaptcha for spam protection. These services can receive technical request information and use browser storage for security and service operation. Rejecting optional analytics does not disable those services.</p><p>Read the <a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy">Web3Forms privacy notice</a> and <a href="https://www.hcaptcha.com/privacy">hCaptcha privacy notice</a>. If you prefer not to use the form, you can email <a href="mailto:hi@replaid.pro">hi@replaid.pro</a> directly.</p></section>
  <section id="app-widget"><h2>The Replaid app and widget</h2><p>The separate Replaid application uses session and security cookies for sign-in and request protection. These are needed for the account functions you request. This website's analytics choice does not sign you out or change application settings.</p><p>When a business installs the Replaid widget on its own website, the widget can store a conversation session token in that website's local storage under a name beginning <code>replaid-widget:</code>. The server-side token expires after 30 days. That expiry is separate from the retention of messages. The business is responsible for its website notices and any consent its use requires.</p></section>
  <section id="browser-controls"><h2>Browser controls</h2><p>You can view, remove, or block cookies and local storage in your browser's privacy settings. Clearing the saved analytics choice makes this website ask again and keeps analytics off until you allow it. Blocking essential storage can affect sign-in, form security, or a widget conversation.</p><p>For requests about data already processed, see the <a href="/privacy/#rights">Privacy Policy</a>. This policy will be updated if the website's storage or providers change.</p></section>
</LegalLayout>
